## 4) What Runs Where (Nomad vs Bare Metal)

**Bare metal**
- Keepalived (VRRP VIP) on Lenovo + Pi5-1.
- PIA WireGuard (ingress) on Lenovo (+ optional on Pi5-1 with failover hooks).
- Consul & Nomad **servers** (Lenovo + both Pi5s).
- Pi-hole + Unbound on both Pi 1s.
- NFS server (Lenovo) & client mount (iMac if Nextcloud runs there).
- **Chef Server (Cinc)** on Lenovo, bound to `127.0.0.1:7443`, behind Traefik **internal**.

**Nomad jobs**
- **Traefik** (Lenovo + Pi5-1), host networking.
- **OpenBao** (iMac), integrated Raft; snapshots to Lenovo.
- **Nextcloud** (iMac if 4GB+; else split with DB on Lenovo), Redis + MariaDB per pattern below.
- **Deluge + VPN sidecar** (Lenovo), WebUI internal-only.
- **Registry + UI** (Lenovo).
- **Observability** (Lenovo): vmagent → VictoriaMetrics, vmalert, Alertmanager, (optional) Loki, Grafana.
- **node_exporter / blackbox_exporter** (system jobs) on Lenovo + Pi5s + iMac (skip Pi1s).
- **Vector/Fluent Bit** (system jobs) on Lenovo + Pi5s + iMac (if enabling Loki).
- **Self-hosted GitHub runners** (Lenovo amd64; Pi5s arm64), **ephemeral**.

